WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:05.310
When you play Elden Ring, you'll inevitably
run up against bosses or areas that will humble

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.310
you.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.310
While it's certainly possible that you've
stumbled into an encounter you're not strong

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.370
enough to face yet, it's important to remember
that a lot of these obstacles are often there

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:10.740
by design.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.469
They do not block the path - they are the
path.

00:00:13.469 --> 00:00:19.000
Through skill, or creativity..or just by coming
back later - you can overcome any obstacle

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.680
in this game, and this video will give you
all the tools you need to do so.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.500
Before you do anything else, you should try
to master the basics of combat.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.900
At the core of combat is your stamina bar,
the green bar under your red health bar.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.550
This resource is depleted when you perform
the actions necessary for fighting.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:41.230
For example, sprinting ... dodging ... blocking
attacks ... attacking ... all of these things,

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:43.060
and more, require stamina.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:50.370
As for the proper flow of combat - While locked
on with R3, keep your shield raised with L1.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:54.750
This will prevent damage from any attacks
that are too fast for you to react to.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:59.060
As you block them, your stamina bar will be
depleted, so make sure to drop your shield

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:03.610
in-between attacks in order to regain that
stamina faster.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:10.210
Now, fast attacks often don't deplete too
much of your stamina - but slow attacks are

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:15.530
a different story, and can easily break your
guard, leaving you wide open.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:21.830
Thus, if you think you can anticipate a slow
attack, it's often better to roll through

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:23.729
it instead.

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:29.570
Rolls have invincibility frames that nullify
all damage if you roll around the instant

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:35.369
where you would have been hit, and while more
difficult to do, avoiding damage in this way

00:01:35.369 --> 00:01:36.570
is much more stamina-efficient.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.390
You should try to wear the heaviest, most
defensive armour you can - but make sure you

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:45.820
stay below 70% equipment load so that your
rolls stay fast and effective.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:51.460
As you fight an enemy, pay special attention
to their animations and try to memorise their

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:52.460
moveset.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:57.220
Over time, you will learn the best way to
avoid certain attacks, and where the openings

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.220
are.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.380
But learn to fight with a mixture of both
blocks, and rolls.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:06.060
As a general rule, you should block fast attacks,
and roll through slow attacks.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:11.779
By fighting efficiently in this way, you'll
avoid damage AND still have stamina left over

00:02:11.779 --> 00:02:15.370
to deal damage while the boss is left open.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:20.719
A new way to deal damage in Elden Ring is
with Guard Counters, which are a core part

00:02:20.719 --> 00:02:25.879
of Elden Ring's combat.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:31.409
Shortly after successfully blocking an attack,
you can retaliate by tapping R2 and performing

00:02:31.409 --> 00:02:33.379
a Guard Counter attack.

00:02:33.379 --> 00:02:35.639
These counters are extremely powerful.

00:02:35.639 --> 00:02:39.590
If you recognise an opportunity to safely
perform one, you should.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:46.010
They deal great damage, and many lesser enemies
will immediately have their Super Armor broken,

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:49.159
opening them up for a critical attack with
R1.

00:02:49.159 --> 00:02:50.769
But what is Super Armor?

00:02:50.769 --> 00:02:54.819
Well, it's an invisible meter that enemies
and bosses have.

00:02:54.819 --> 00:03:00.129
It depletes when they take damage, and when
you fully deplete it and break their Super

00:03:00.129 --> 00:03:05.439
Armor, you can perform a critical attack by
tapping R1.

00:03:05.439 --> 00:03:10.170
As a rule of thumb, any R2 attack will do
more Super Armor damage.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:15.790
Jumping R2 attacks do a lot ... Running R2
attacks are great too ... but fully charged

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:18.769
R2 attacks seem to do the most.

00:03:18.769 --> 00:03:22.279
Also worth noting is that Super Armor regenerates
over time.

00:03:22.279 --> 00:03:26.629
Therefore, it's important that you continually
deal damage to your enemies.

00:03:26.629 --> 00:03:35.329
If you sense a boss is close to breaking point,
go on the offensive with your R2 attacks.

00:03:35.329 --> 00:03:38.450
Often, you'll be rewarded.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:42.839
On the other hand, if you're simply just looking
to do consistent damage - well, tapping R1

00:03:42.839 --> 00:03:45.060
is the probably the way to go.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:52.049
R1 attacks generally come out much faster,
and aren't as risky to perform.

00:03:52.049 --> 00:03:57.199
If you really want to prioritise damage over
defense, then you can two-hand your weapon.

00:03:57.199 --> 00:04:03.959
The input for this is to hold Triangle or
Y, and tap R1 or L1 to two-hand your right-hand

00:04:03.959 --> 00:04:06.540
item, or left-hand item, respectively.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:11.639
In addition to granting you a new moveset,
you will have more strength, more damage,

00:04:11.639 --> 00:04:16.940
more super armor damage, and you can also
often avoid recoil when striking an enemy's

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:17.940
shield.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.590
So if your shield isn't helping much with
an encounter, consider two-handing for damage

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:23.900
instead.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:29.530
While you'll mostly be dodging for defense
in this state, it's worth noting that you

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:37.430
can still block while two-handing, and while
you'll take some chip damage - it's still

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:44.880
a good idea to block in many situations, especially
if you want to utilise guard counters.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.670
Another offensive alternative to two-handing
is powerstancing, which can be achieved by

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:53.510
equipping two weapons of the same class, one
in each hand.

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:58.880
With this, you'll get access to a special
L1 attack that utilises both weapons.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:04.410
Just like your R1 attacks, your L1 attacks
do a combo of attacks, and can be utilised

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:07.150
in jumping attacks as well.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:12.040
Speaking of jumping attacks, they are incredible
gap closers, allowing you to cover distance

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.150
and queue an attack simultaneously.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:19.710
If an enemy is left open, but you're far away
- close the distance with a jumping attack

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:22.220
to see how effective they can be.

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:27.380
Jumping R1 attacks are generally better for
flying or mounted enemies... and jumping R2

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:32.810
attacks are generally better if you want to
inflict damage and posture damage upon grounded

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.050
enemies.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:38.920
Damage can be healed with your Flask of Crimson
Tears, which will always replenish when you

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:41.510
warp, or sit at a grace checkpoint.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:46.740
Additionally, you can get extra flask charges
by clearing out a group of enemies ... or

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:50.580
by defeating these small red creatures.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:55.560
At grace checkpoints, you can upgrade your
flask with Golden Seeds and Sacred Tears.

00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:00.500
Golden seeds are found at minor erdtrees,
and increase the amount of flasks you can

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.500
carry.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:07.590
Sacred Tears are found at Churches of Marika,
and increase the amount healed by your flasks.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:13.300
Furthermore, you can balance the allotment
of crimson flasks and cerulean flasks you

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:16.960
carry at a site of grace, to better suit your
needs.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:21.610
To quickly access your crimson healing flask
at any time, consider making it the first

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.460
item on your quick-select bar.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:28.580
This way, if you hold down on the d-pad, you'll
always shortcut to it instantly.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:33.950
At the top of the d-pad, you'll be able to
cycle through your current selection of spells.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.920
New spells can be memorized at a site of grace.

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:42.770
These spells will either be incantations,
which must be cast with an equipped seal...or

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:45.990
sorceries, which must be cast with an equipped
staff.

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:50.930
Cycle through your equipped armaments by pressing
left or right on the d-pad.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:54.520
If you die, then you'll drop all your runes
at your point of death.

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:58.639
If you don't pick them up during your next
life, then they'll be gone forever.

00:06:58.639 --> 00:07:05.460
Make sure to seek them out using your compass,
whenever you can.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:10.220
When you do die, you can choose to resurrect
at a site of grace, or sometimes at a Stake

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:11.550
of Marika.

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:16.860
If you see this statue ... or this icon, then
it's probably an indication that you're in

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:22.100
a difficult area, or near a boss, as a Stake
of Marika is nearby.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:27.150
Respawning at a Stake of Marika will usually
make your run back to your runes less severe,

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:31.880
so it's often best to choose that option,
unless you'd prefer to move on from what killed

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:32.880
you.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:37.070
If you're out in the open world, one way to
overcome difficulty is by choosing the right

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:38.910
scenarios to fight on your mount.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:40.150
You'll receive your mount after visiting your
third site of lost grace.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:45.320
Against large or mounted enemies that struggle
against hit and run tactics, the mount is

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.400
definitely the way to go.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:53.270
While mounted, R1 and R2 give you light and
heavy attacks on the right side, and L1 and

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:56.870
L2 give light and heavy attacks on your left
side.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:02.840
If you hold your heavy attacks, you can charge
them up, dealing continuous damage while you

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:06.340
charge, culminating in a strong attack at
the end.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:10.360
While mounted, you automatically wield the
armament in your right hand.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:14.690
If you would prefer to wield the armament
in your left hand, use a two-handing input

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:19.800
- so hold triangle or Y, and tap L1 or R1.

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:24.470
Torrent can take damage separately from the
player, but his damage can be healed by your

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:27.730
crimson flasks, as well as craftable rowa
raisins.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:28.730
If he does somehow die before you, then you'll
have to sacrifice a crimson flask to revive

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:29.730
him.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:33.079
As you get hit on your mount, you run the
risk of losing your posture and getting knocked

00:08:33.079 --> 00:08:35.659
down for an extended period of time.

00:08:35.659 --> 00:08:38.759
If this happens, you are extremely vulnerable.

00:08:38.759 --> 00:08:43.110
If you're taking damage, then at a certain
point, no matter what you're fighting, it's

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:47.769
probably wise to dismount and fight them on
foot for a while.

00:08:47.769 --> 00:08:52.420
Jumping attacks off your horse are a great
way to transition into melee combat.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:56.670
Dismount with L3, and slam them with L1, R1,
or R2.

00:08:56.670 --> 00:09:01.449
The distance you cover with this is absurd,
and initiating a fight in this way gives you

00:09:01.449 --> 00:09:03.380
an immediate advantage.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:08.089
As the fight goes on, consider if mounting
up again for a burst of speed would be to

00:09:08.089 --> 00:09:09.389
your benefit.

00:09:09.389 --> 00:09:13.670
Against Flying Dragon Agheel, for example,
certain attacks are better off being outpaced

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:15.389
on a mount.

00:09:15.389 --> 00:09:20.790
For a reliable way to mount up quickly, I
would recommend binding your Spectral Steed

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:26.339
Whistle to your pouch - a secondary D-pad
menu that can be edited in the menu screen.

00:09:26.339 --> 00:09:31.400
You can quickly access these all four of these
bindings by holding down triangle or Y, then

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.820
tapping the appropriate d-pad button.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:38.309
This way, you'll have a consistent input for
mounting up, instead of toggling rapidly through

00:09:38.309 --> 00:09:40.519
your items looking for your Spectral Steed
Whistle.

00:09:40.519 --> 00:09:48.459
This same logic applies to any other item
you want quick, reliable access to.

00:09:48.459 --> 00:09:52.569
In addition to your double jump for extra
height, be on the lookout for Spirit Springs,

00:09:52.569 --> 00:09:55.240
which take you to incredible heights.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:10:00.720
Conversely, you can safely jump into a spirit
spring to negate all fall damage.

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:06.589
While on your mount, L3 dismounts you...but
when on foot, L3 will be used for stealth.

00:10:06.589 --> 00:10:11.399
In this crouched state, enemy aggro range
is reduced, and you'll have an easier time

00:10:11.399 --> 00:10:13.740
getting R1 backstabs.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:19.089
Enemy aggro range is also reduced at night,
so consider passing time at a site of grace

00:10:19.089 --> 00:10:20.779
to better suit your needs.

00:10:20.779 --> 00:10:25.819
At night, however, you might also find different
enemies spawning in the world, so be aware

00:10:25.819 --> 00:10:26.819
of that.

00:10:26.819 --> 00:10:31.230
Another thing to get in the habit of is crafting,
which you can do as soon as you buy the crafting

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:34.629
kit from Kale at the Church of Elleh.

00:10:34.629 --> 00:10:39.240
After this, the crafting tab in your menu
screen will unlock for use.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:43.579
After a few hours of play, you should have
accumulated a few recipe books to expand your

00:10:43.579 --> 00:10:48.540
crafting options, and if you've been hunting
and foraging between bosses, then you'll be

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:51.180
able to make a lot of great items.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:55.709
Pay attention to which material drops you
find in the world: It'll make it that tiny

00:10:55.709 --> 00:11:00.959
bit easier to gather more of it when you realise
you need it to craft something specific.

00:11:00.959 --> 00:11:05.540
The crafting page gives you hints at where
to find specific materials, and most world

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:11.410
materials respawn instantly upon resting at
a grace, making them fairly easy to farm.

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:16.329
Oh, and while you're at Kale - grab a torch
to help you see in dark caves.

00:11:16.329 --> 00:11:21.760
When you find one of his fellow merchants
on a beach southwest of the Church of Elleh-

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.839
grab a bow, as well.

00:11:23.839 --> 00:11:29.809
Ranged weapons are excellent utility tools,
allowing you to lure, poison, or sleep enemies

00:11:29.809 --> 00:11:30.809
from afar.

00:11:30.809 --> 00:11:37.890
There are two types of bow weapons - bows,
and crossbows, which use arrows or bolts respectively.

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:42.629
Enter Precision Aiming mode with L1 while
two-handing the bow, and press r1 to fire

00:11:42.629 --> 00:11:52.079
the projectile in the first slot, and R2 to
fire the projectile in the second slot.

00:11:52.079 --> 00:12:02.410
If you feel your damage is too low, then the
easiest way to deal more is to reinforce your

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:06.620
weapon, which can be done at the Church of
Elleh at the smithing table.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:12.529
Here, you'll be able to get most armaments
to +3 here with smithing stone shards found

00:12:12.529 --> 00:12:13.720
around the world.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:19.690
That said, special armaments require other,
special shards...and to go beyond +3, you'll

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:22.230
need to find an actual blacksmith.

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:26.559
Alternatively, if you aren't happy with your
shield - take a look at its stats.

00:12:26.559 --> 00:12:31.740
The most reliable shields are those that block
100% physical damage, but you can consider

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:34.929
switching shields to suit specific encounters.

00:12:34.929 --> 00:12:38.050
The other stat you're looking at, is stability.

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:41.680
Higher stability means you'll take less of
a stamina hit when you block.

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:43.100
To raise this, choose a different shield,
or reinforce it, just like you did your weapons.

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:45.319
Upgrading an armamentn is bit of a commitment.

00:12:45.319 --> 00:12:49.959
You can always find more smithing stone shards
in caves, and around the world ... but these

00:12:49.959 --> 00:12:55.379
are fairly rare, so make sure you really enjoy
swinging your weapon, before upgrading it.

00:12:55.379 --> 00:12:59.029
Of course, a weapon also has to suit your
build.

00:12:59.029 --> 00:13:04.690
Your build is determined by what stats you
level at Grace checkpoints by summoning Melina,

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:07.129
and investing your runes with her.

00:13:07.129 --> 00:13:10.499
When you start the game, you'll have to choose
a starting character.

00:13:10.499 --> 00:13:15.369
Some use magic, some have ranged weapons,
and some excel in melee - but it's important

00:13:15.369 --> 00:13:19.079
to remember that your starting class doesn't
dictate your build.

00:13:19.079 --> 00:13:20.079
You do.

00:13:20.079 --> 00:13:24.560
While each characters starting stats give
them different strengths and weaknesses, you

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:28.550
are free to build your character in a different
direction.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:33.779
If you haven't settled on a build yet, then
you can't go too wrong by levelling Vigor

00:13:33.779 --> 00:13:40.170
for HP and resistance...Endurance for Stamina
and equipment load...or Mind to increase your

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:45.879
FP - but it's the other stats that make a
real impact on your character archetype.

00:13:45.879 --> 00:13:51.050
Strength, for example, mostly affects your
ability to wield heavy armaments, as well

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:52.559
as your defense.

00:13:52.559 --> 00:13:56.980
Strength weapons are often slow, so being
a bit more tanky will come in handy.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:14:02.069
Another stat to look out for is poise, which
will raise as you put on heavier armour.

00:14:02.069 --> 00:14:08.149
Having high poise will often prevent you getting
interrupted mid-attack.

00:14:08.149 --> 00:14:13.050
Dexterity is the counterpart to strength,
and raises your ability to wield a lot of

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:15.949
lighter armaments, boosting their attack power.

00:14:15.949 --> 00:14:21.019
It also softens fall damage, makes it harder
to be knocked off your horse, and reduces

00:14:21.019 --> 00:14:23.680
the cast-time of spells.

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:27.600
Spells usually scale in damage with Intelligence
or Faith.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:32.339
Intelligence generally boosts the damage of
sorceries, while Faith generally boosts the

00:14:32.339 --> 00:14:35.509
damage and healing of incantations.

00:14:35.509 --> 00:14:41.059
Arcane is a new attribute in Elden Ring, and
it governs your discovery stat, which increases

00:14:41.059 --> 00:14:42.949
enemy item drop rate.

00:14:42.949 --> 00:14:47.850
It's also a stat that increases the damage
of certain sorceries and incantations, and

00:14:47.850 --> 00:14:51.209
can play into the stat scaling of certain
weapons.

00:14:51.209 --> 00:15:00.410
Every weapon comes with a default scaling,
which you can view here.

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:05.050
However, applying an Ash of War to your weapon
often allows you to choose a more beneficial

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:09.879
damage type and scaling option for that weapon.

00:15:09.879 --> 00:15:15.320
Beyond their scaling options, Ashes of War
can be used to apply skills to your armaments.

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:20.329
Once applied, L2 will unleash their effects
- and you can always see which Skill you will

00:15:20.329 --> 00:15:22.949
perform with L2, here.

00:15:22.949 --> 00:15:27.749
To apply an Ash of War, be sure to pick up
the Whetstone Knife in a cellar at the Gatefront

00:15:27.749 --> 00:15:28.949
Ruins.

00:15:28.949 --> 00:15:32.680
After this, sit at a grace checkpoint, and
experiment with your options.

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:38.350
Often, these skills will default to your shields'
applied Ash of War, unless you two-hand your

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:41.720
weapon, or use a shield without a special
skill.

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:47.329
These attacks are very powerful, and require
a small amount of Focus Points to use.

00:15:47.329 --> 00:15:51.209
Your FP is represented here, in this blue
bar.

00:15:51.209 --> 00:15:57.220
This is a valuable resource - especially for
magic builds, which also rely on it to cast

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:58.220
spells.

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:03.939
That said, ALL builds can, and should, find
a use for FP, and if you're having trouble

00:16:03.939 --> 00:16:10.040
in Elden Ring, you should always be thinking
of an effective way to make use of this resource.

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:13.899
Another powerful way to make use of FP is
by summoning spirits.

00:16:13.899 --> 00:16:17.679
Once you acquire the summoning bell early
in the game, you'll be able to equip spirits

00:16:17.679 --> 00:16:21.749
on your quick-select bar and summon them for
difficult encounters.

00:16:21.749 --> 00:16:27.000
As long as you have enough FP, and as long
as this "rebirth monument" symbol marks the

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:32.259
encounter as difficult, then your spirits
will fight alongside you until death.

00:16:32.259 --> 00:16:35.819
Some are ranged attackers, some are tanky,
and some are a combination of both.

00:16:35.819 --> 00:16:40.110
Decide what works best for your build, and
the encounter.

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:45.589
Only one type of spirit can be summoned at
a time, and spirits cannot be summoned during

00:16:45.589 --> 00:16:46.990
multiplayer.

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:50.920
Speaking of multiplayer - if you're truly
having trouble, be on the lookout for Furlcalling

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:54.619
Finger Remedies, which you can find throughout
the world.

00:16:54.619 --> 00:16:58.910
Once consumed, these allow you to see other
players' summon signs and summon help for

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:00.600
major encounters.

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:05.750
That said, you'll always be able to see NPC
summon signs, so feel free to make good use

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:06.750
of them.

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:11.830
Alternatively, other players' signs can be
accessed in summoning pools located at summoning

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:15.000
effigies that are placed in key areas.

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:19.250
If you want to learn more about engaging in
multiplayer, read the items on your multiplayer

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:25.610
tab in the menu screen.

00:17:25.610 --> 00:17:32.750
Last, but not least, your map.

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:37.560
Revealing the map for an area will make it
much easier to progress through the game.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:41.590
Map fragments can be collected at these glowing
Guide Stele's.

00:17:41.590 --> 00:17:45.780
If you're having trouble finding one in an
unfamiliar area, try to stick to the main

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:51.590
path - or, failing that, try to look for this
shape on your undiscovered map.

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:55.680
With the map open, you can mark points of
interest with markers, or beacons that show

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:57.310
up in the overworld.

00:17:57.310 --> 00:18:01.630
You can also fast-travel between sites of
lost Grace, and get a clearer idea of the

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:04.390
direction that the main story requires.

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:08.540
Rays of light will guide you on that path,
and often lead you towards your next logical

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:09.540
checkpoint.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:14.300
Of course, it's up to you whether you want
to trust the guidance of grace.

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:18.250
If you're having trouble with the main path
- go in the opposite direction.

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:19.250
Explore.

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:20.250
Get stronger.

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:21.990
Learn how to master your build.

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:25.060
The guidance of grace can often be spurned,
to great effect.

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:26.270
Thank you for listening.

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:32.580
If you'd like to learn more, you can find
me on YouTube at youtube.com/vaatividya, and

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:36.160
I wish you all the best in overcoming difficulty
in Elden Ring.

